Cut 2026-09-28 on Anthony's word ("Yes, cut 0.74.0"), for combined-plan position 6. One built change since v0.73.0:
- The `hub` skill (/hub, #612, chg:a-hub-skill-files-each-fact-where-it-belongs-2026-09-28). For a session that reaches a hub and the designs it coordinates (a flo2.io hub design, a local hub like dev_reflow2, or an agent holding several design addresses), it:
  - reads a child design only when a request needs it;
  - writes each fact to the lowest design that owns all of it, naming that design first;
  - keeps a collaborator's idea in the hub until someone who can write to the right design routes it, leaving a ROUTED pointer in the hub.
Why now: flo2's shared hubs (flo2 #98, epoch:shared-hubs) point every hub at this skill, at both of flo2's doors. flo2.io upgrades to this release before #98 deploys. MINOR, as a new skill; the schema stamp is unmoved.
